.json"} {"question" "q-139960" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+8y=-14 \\\\ 5x+4y=13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "315f98713864cf7d17ffc252fe9128bf9f8f8ff78019fc93f45a94227ddbc43b" "basis" 1856 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-139960" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+8y=-14 \\\\ 5x+4y=13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$ we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -14 \\\\ 5 & 13\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -14 \\\\ 5 & 13\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "315f98713864cf7d17ffc252fe9128bf9f8f8ff78019fc93f45a94227ddbc43b" "basis" 1856 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-139960" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/questio