l/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "315f98713864cf7d17ffc252fe9128bf9f8f8ff78019fc93f45a94227ddbc43b" "basis" 1856 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-42970" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+7y=13 \\\\ -2x+5y=19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$ we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 13 \\\\ -2 & 19\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 13 \\\\ -2 & 19\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/state.json" "file_sha256" "315f98713864cf7d17ffc252fe9128bf9f8f8ff78019fc93f45a94227ddbc43b" "basis" 1856 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-42970" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdb98914303911996d27ba6ad272178e6a8b8b2a5eaa5abf591d823574ec8381" "basis" 1856 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-42970" "field" "select